course: dictionary
lesson: 6636
title: Words that compare now and then
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nowadays is a time word. It tells the reader that something is true at the present time, and it often compares now with the past. In a history lesson you might read: «In Victorian times children worked in factories; nowadays they go to school.» The word nowadays shows that the writer is comparing then with now.
explain: Look for the comparison. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about now, or about the past? In «the best flats get picked up so quickly nowadays», the field-mouse is saying that flats are sold fast today, which is a comparison with how things used to be.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap «nowadays» for «at the present time» and read it again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right. Nowadays is an adverb, so it tells us about when something happens.
fact: Nowadays means at the present time, compared with the past.
fact: «Nowadays» is an adverb, a word that tells us about time, place or how something happens.
fact: In «before those horrid machines begin clicking round the fields», the mouse is warning about machines that are coming soon.
fact: In «the best flats get picked up so quickly nowadays», nowadays compares today with the past.
fact: Writers use «nowadays» in history and everyday talk to show a change between then and now.
exercise: «The best flats get picked up so quickly nowadays.» What does nowadays mean here? | Tomorrow, in the future | Long ago, in the past | Only early in the morning | *At the present time, compared with the past
exercise: Find and copy the word in this sentence that means at the present time: «The best flats get picked up so quickly nowadays.» | *nowadays | quickly | picked | flats
exercise: «In Victorian times children worked in factories; nowadays they go to school.» What does nowadays show? | Only the Victorian times are being described | A plan for next year | *The writer is comparing the past with now | A made-up story about a mouse
test: «Nowadays many homes have central heating, but long ago people sat by open fires.» Which word shows the comparison? | Homes | *Nowadays | Central | Fires
test: What does «nowadays» tell the reader in «the best flats get picked up so quickly nowadays»? | *It compares now with the past: flats sell faster today | It is a magic spell | It means quickly and quietly | It means the flats are very old
exam: Nowadays is an adverb. Which word means at the present time, compared with the past? | *nowadays | flats | quickly | machines
